sentences.l:
And the two, then, having sprung up, Odysseus and his glorious son,
began to carry in helmets and shields with bosses
and sharp spears;

So he spoke, and Telemachus through the hall had gone,
wishing to lie down, to a chamber, under flaring torches,
where before he used to sleep, whenever sweet sleep might come on him;

Such are beggars and vagrant men;
for I too once a house among men inhabited,
prosperous, a rich one, and often I used to give to a vagrant,
to one such as he might be and of whatever in need he might come;

But if he, indeed, has so perished and is no longer one to come home,
yet already a son is such, by Apollo’s will at least,
Telemachus;

“Eurynome, bring now a stool and a fleece upon it,
so that, sitting down, he may say his word and hear,
the stranger, me;
